 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send web push notifications to people's phones and desktops whenever something new lands in their notifications tray.
+To enable them, you need to provide a VAPID key pair.
+You can generate one inside the container with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set both environment variables:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BD... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=5G... ...
+```
+
+Without these keys, push notifications are disabled and the option to turn them on is hidden from the notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
